    "description": "On the home network, the phone's first frame is one byte saying how it opens (1 keys, 2 code, 3 token, 4 qr) then that handshake's first message. keys: Noise IK as in handshake, with this prologue. code, token and qr: CPace (CPACE-X25519-SHA512, initiator-responder, sid empty, ADb empty), then (k1, k2) = HKDF-SHA256(salt keysSalt, ISK) split as Noise does, k1 for the phone's records. token: prs = SHA-256 of the token's UTF-8, ada = the phone's id, first 16 bytes of SHA-256('kiko phone id v1' || 0x00 || prs). qr: prs = the QR code's 16-byte secret, ada = the code's id, first 16 bytes of SHA-256('kiko qr id v1' || 0x00 || secret); url is the pairing URL the code carries (relayUrl: with the relay), and symbol the QR code the Mac makes of url (rows top to bottom, 1 dark, no quiet zone); relayCredential = SHA-256('kiko qr relay v1' || 0x00 || secret), what a phone away from home joins the Mac's room with to pair by the code (relayJoin; the relay keeps only relayCredentialHash, which the Mac registers: relayPairing), then the same first frame as at home, through the relay. cpaceDraft: draft-irtf-cfrg-cpace-21's own vector B.1.",
